Package: vennabers
Title: Venn-Abers Classification and Regression Calibration
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("René-M.", "Kruse", email = "rene.marcel.kruse@protonmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Fits binary Inductive and Cross Venn-Abers calibrators from
    caller-supplied probabilities. Returns Inductive Venn-Abers intervals
    and regularized probabilities, or Cross Venn-Abers regularized
    probabilities using equal-weight aggregation across matched folds.
    Supports log-loss or Brier regularization, calibration probability
    rounding, binary class predictions, and individual fold results.
    Supports manual Inductive and Cross multiclass one-vs-one and one-vs-rest calibration
    with named class probabilities and binary diagnostics. Includes binary and multiclass
    Brier score and log loss, fit diagnoses that plot stored calibration maps,
    and CORP reliability diagrams with resampling uncertainty bands as
    described in Dimitriadis, Gneiting and Jordan (2021)
    <doi:10.1073/pnas.2016191118>. Fits moderated
    Inductive and Cross regression calibrators from supplied real-valued
    predictions, returning regression bounds and weighted Inductive point
    predictions or equal-weight means of complete fold results. Optional
    native 'tidymodels' workflows train complete local preprocessing and
    models for binary, one-vs-one, one-vs-rest and regression calibration,
    with Inductive or Cross splits and complete outer resampling, joint or
    two-stage Grid/Bayes selection, and learned Sigmoid, 'tailor' or
    reference isotonic postprocessing on separate holdouts or inner ensembles.
    Inductive training and calibration sizes can be set independently, own
    model fit and predict functions can serve as workflow models, and class
    decisions can be represented as one-hot matrices.
    Venn-Abers predictors are described in Vovk and Petej (2014)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1211.0025>; Inductive and Cross Venn-Abers
    predictors in Vovk, Petej and Fedorova (2015)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1511.00213>. One-vs-one multiclass calibration
    couples the pairwise Inductive or Cross Venn-Abers probabilities as in
    Manokhin (2017) <https://proceedings.mlr.press/v60/manokhin17a.html>.
    This independent R implementation checks its shared core results
    against reference outputs of the 'Python' package 'venn-abers'; the
    installed file PARITY.md separates numerical parity from R extensions
    and documented deviations.
